15. Why this architecture is good
It prevents:
P3 POTENTIAL
     ↓
automatic exploitation

Instead:
P3 POTENTIAL
     ↓
P4 VALIDATION
     ↓
CONFIRMED
     ↓
EXPLOITATION GATE
     ↓
controlled exploitation

So Project 4 isn't just:
"Run payload."

It is:
Validate first, then permit controlled impact demonstration only when the finding passes the required gates.

16. Exploitation must remain bounded
The current Project 4 code has:
max_validation_requests = 10
max_exploitation_requests = 5

and an ActionBudget.
An exploitation action also checks that:
- URL is HTTP/HTTPS
- URL has a hostname
- hostname matches authorized target
- port matches where applicable
- credentials aren't embedded in URL
- strategy exists
- action matches the strategy
So exploitation is not supposed to become an unrestricted attack engine.
